Reorganize graph functions

This commit reorganizes the existing graph functions by
1. moving their implementation to a separate header file, for the sake
   of keeping abstract_graph.hpp easy to read;
2. making the functions to compute distances member functions of
   AbstractGraph for consistency with the BFS methods;
3. implementing Distances in terms of the generic BFS method;
4. moving the code for all-pairs distances to AbstractGraph.

Better docs (#1299)

All experimental section of the docs was with broken links. This fixes it.

@femtobit this creates actual docstrings for our integrators which otherwise where.. undocumented. Can you give a look?

void FindConn(VectorConstRefType v, std::vector<Complex> &mel,
              std::vector<std::vector<int>> &connectors,
              std::vector<std::vector<double>> &newconfs) const override {
  return this->FindConn(v, mel, connectors, newconfs, true);
}

Reorganize graph functions

This commit reorganizes the existing graph functions by
1. moving their implementation to a separate header file, for the sake
   of keeping abstract_graph.hpp easy to read;
2. making the functions to compute distances member functions of
   AbstractGraph for consistency with the BFS methods;
3. implementing Distances in terms of the generic BFS method;
4. moving the code for all-pairs distances to AbstractGraph.

Bug when using big endian transfer syntax

When writing big endian lengths the bytes were not reversed.

var pathToDicom = @"...";
var dicom = DICOMFileReader.Read(pathToDicom);
var bigEndian = new DICOMWriteSettings
{
    TransferSyntax = TransferSyntax.EXPLICIT_VR_BIG_ENDIAN
};
DICOMFileWriter.Write(pathToDicom, bigEndian, dicom);

Also removed the unused WriteBigEndian stub and switched from Enumerable.Reverse to the more efficient Array.Reverse.

1. DICOMData add ToString method that can specify split symbol when has multipicityValue;
2. DICOMObject add FindPublicFirst method that can filter private sequences and their elements
3. add elements read unit tests and test resource
